#: ../../../file_formats/specfile.rst:-1
msgid ""
"A developer reference for the Spack spec file format, describing its "
"structure, how the DAG hash is computed, its compatibility across releases, "
"and its version history."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/specfile.rst:13
msgid "Spec File Format"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/specfile.rst:15
msgid ""
"This document describes the spec file format, which stores the DAG of a spec "
"as JSON. The current version of the format is |specfile_format_version|, "
"defined by :data:`spack.spec.SPECFILE_FORMAT_VERSION`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/specfile.rst:18
msgid "Spec files are found in the following places:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/specfile.rst:20
msgid ""
"In ``<prefix>/.spack/spec.json``, written when a spec is installed. ``spack "
"reindex`` rebuilds the Database from these files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/specfile.rst:22
msgid ""
"In build caches, where a few keys specific to build caches are added to the "
"spec file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/specfile.rst:23
msgid "In the output of ``spack spec --json``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/specfile.rst:25
msgid ""
"The Database and the lockfile store the nodes of a spec file without the "
"enclosing ``spec`` and ``_meta`` keys, as described in :ref:`file-formats`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/specfile.rst:27
msgid ""
"All of these files hold concrete specs, and the rest of this document "
"describes concrete specs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/specfile.rst:29
msgid "Abstract specs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/specfile.rst:32
msgid ""
"The format can also represent abstract specs, which are written only in the "
"entries of the concretization cache, for troubleshooting, and are not read "
"back. The nodes of an abstract spec have ``\"concrete\": false``, and may "
"have the keys ``abstract_hash``, ``compiler_flags``, ``propagate``, "
"``abstract``, ``propagated_parameters``, and ``propagated_abstract``; their "
"dependencies may have ``when`` and ``propagation``. None of these keys is "
"written for concrete specs, so they do not affect the DAG hash."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/specfile.rst:37
msgid "Structure"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/specfile.rst:39
msgid ""
"This section describes the current version of the format, |"
"specfile_format_version|. A spec file has a single top-level ``spec`` key, "
"which holds the version of the format and the list of nodes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/specfile.rst:42
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"spec\": {\n"
"    \"_meta\": {\"version\": 6},\n"
"    \"nodes\": [\n"
"      {\n"
"        \"name\": \"zlib-ng\",\n"
"        \"version\": \"2.3.3\",\n"
"        \"arch\": {\"platform\": \"linux\", \"platform_os\": "
"\"ubuntu24.04\", \"target\": {\"name\": \"alderlake\"}},\n"
"        \"namespace\": \"builtin\",\n"
"        \"parameters\": {\"build_system\": \"autotools\", \"shared\": true, "
"\"cflags\": []},\n"
"        \"package_hash\": "
"\"bnbx7ezlmmjgjyubhncgeel7lpbjrj6l4aeuhyewdeyz56l7tqsq====\",\n"
"        \"provided_virtuals\": [\"zlib-api\"],\n"
"        \"dependencies\": [\n"
"          {\n"
"            \"name\": \"gcc\",\n"
"            \"hash\": \"26zpexhcroz5n23vbzm5ypre7tlfus2b\",\n"
"            \"parameters\": {\"deptypes\": [\"build\"], \"virtuals\": "
"[\"c\", \"cxx\"]}\n"
"          },\n"
"          {\n"
"            \"name\": \"glibc\",\n"
"            \"hash\": \"cyucshxqmd4krmsp7nco25trnybrdbam\",\n"
"            \"parameters\": {\"deptypes\": [\"link\"], \"virtuals\": "
"[\"libc\"]}\n"
"          }\n"
"        ],\n"
"        \"annotations\": {\"original_specfile_version\": 6},\n"
"        \"hash\": \"nic37xsihlqze3xyg3xd6pthcgqxoy6p\"\n"
"      }\n"
"    ]\n"
"  }\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/specfile.rst:75
msgid ""
"To keep the example short, the features of the target, most variants, the "
"remaining dependencies, and the remaining nodes are not shown."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/specfile.rst:77
msgid ""
"The first node of the list is the root of the DAG. The order of the "
"remaining nodes is not significant, since nodes refer to each other by hash. "
"Each node is listed once, even if it can be reached through several paths. "
"For a spliced spec, the list also includes the nodes of the build spec."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/specfile.rst:82
msgid ""
"Each node is a dictionary with the following keys. The keys of previous "
"versions are described in :ref:`specfile-version-history`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/specfile.rst:85
msgid "``name``, ``version``, ``arch``, ``namespace``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/specfile.rst:86
msgid "The identity of the node."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/specfile.rst:87
msgid "``parameters``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/specfile.rst:88
msgid "The values of the variants, and the compiler flags."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/specfile.rst:89
msgid "``patches``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/specfile.rst:90
msgid ""
"The hashes of the patches applied to the node, in the order in which they "
"are applied. It is present only in nodes that have patches."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/specfile.rst:92
msgid "``package_hash``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/specfile.rst:93
msgid ""
"The hash of the content of the ``package.py`` that the node was concretized "
"with."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/specfile.rst:94
msgid "``provided_virtuals``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/specfile.rst:95
msgid ""
"The virtuals that a concrete node provides, possibly with a version, for "
"instance ``libgfortran@5``. It is written only when the node provides at "
"least one virtual."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/specfile.rst:97
msgid "``dependencies``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/specfile.rst:98
msgid ""
"One entry for each edge, which refers to the dependency by name and DAG "
"hash. The ``parameters`` of the entry hold the dependency types, the "
"virtuals that the dependency provides on that edge, and ``direct: true`` for "
"direct dependencies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/specfile.rst:100
msgid "``build_spec``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/specfile.rst:101
msgid ""
"The name and DAG hash of the spec that was built. It is present only in "
"spliced specs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/specfile.rst:103
msgid "``external``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/specfile.rst:104
msgid ""
"The path or the modules of an external, and its extra attributes. It is "
"present only in externals."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/specfile.rst:106
msgid "``annotations``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/specfile.rst:107
msgid ""
"``original_specfile_version`` is the version of the spec file from which the "
"node was first read. Nodes first read from a spec file before v5 also have "
"``compiler``, the compiler that those versions stored as a node attribute."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/specfile.rst:109
msgid "``hash``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/specfile.rst:110
msgid "The DAG hash of the node."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/specfile.rst:112
msgid "A JSON schema of the format is in ``lib/spack/spack/schema/spec.py``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/specfile.rst:115
msgid "How the DAG Hash Is Computed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/specfile.rst:117
msgid "The DAG hash of a concrete node is computed in two steps:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/specfile.rst:119
msgid ""
"The node dictionary, without the ``hash`` key, is serialized as JSON with no "
"whitespace, and with the keys in the order in which they are written."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/specfile.rst:120
msgid ""
"The SHA-1 digest of the serialization is encoded in base32, in lowercase."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/specfile.rst:122
msgid "This definition has the following consequences:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/specfile.rst:124
msgid ""
"The node dictionary contains the hashes of the dependencies, so the DAG hash "
"depends on the entire sub-DAG."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/specfile.rst:125
msgid ""
"Any change to what Spack writes for a concrete node, including the order of "
"its keys, gives a different hash to every spec concretized afterwards."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/specfile.rst:127
msgid ""
"The hash stored in a spec file is never recomputed when the file is read. "
"Spack can therefore read a spec written with an older definition of the "
"hash, and still find the installation it refers to. The changes to the "
"definition are listed in :ref:`specfile-version-history`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/specfile.rst:132
msgid "Spliced specs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/specfile.rst:133
msgid ""
"The hash of a spliced spec is computed in the same way, except that its last "
"7 characters are replaced by those of the hash of its build spec. A spliced "
"spec is installed by relocating the binaries of its build spec to a new "
"prefix, and relocation has to leave the end of the prefix unchanged. The "
"reason is that compilers save space by storing a string constant as the "
"suffix of a longer one, so rewriting the end of a path in a binary could "
"alter an unrelated string that shares it. With the default layout the prefix "
"ends with the hash, hence the two hashes have the same ending."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/specfile.rst:139
msgid "Compatibility"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/specfile.rst:141
msgid "The properties below are defined in :ref:`file-formats`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/specfile.rst:143
msgid "**Backward compatibility**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/specfile.rst:144
msgid ""
"Every version of Spack reads all the versions of the format up to its own. "
"When reading an older version, Spack reconstructs the information that the "
"version does not store from the package repositories."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/specfile.rst:147
msgid "**Forward compatibility**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/specfile.rst:148
msgid "None. Reading a version newer than the current one is an error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/specfile.rst:151
msgid "**Rewrite policy**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/specfile.rst:152
msgid ""
"Spec files are never rewritten. The ``spec.json`` file of an installation "
"prefix remains in the version it was written in. When a node read from an "
"older version is written to a new file, its original version is recorded in "
"``annotations.original_specfile_version``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/specfile.rst:159
msgid "Version History"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/specfile.rst:161
msgid ""
"The version is recorded in ``spec._meta.version``. Spec files in version 1 "
"have no ``_meta`` key, and are recognized because their ``spec`` key holds a "
"list."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/specfile.rst:164
msgid "**Version 6** *(Spack v1.3)*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/specfile.rst:165
msgid ""
"Concrete nodes record the virtuals they provide in ``provided_virtuals``, "
"which is part of the DAG hash (`#53012 <https://github.com/spack/spack/"
"pull/53012>`_)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/specfile.rst:167
msgid "**Version 5** *(Spack v1.0)*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/specfile.rst:168
msgid ""
"Compilers become build dependencies (`#45189 <https://github.com/spack/spack/"
"pull/45189>`_). The ``compiler`` attribute of nodes is removed, "
"``annotations`` is added, and ``parameters.direct`` marks direct "
"dependencies. From Spack v1.0 on, the DAG hash also includes test "
"dependencies (`#49505 <https://github.com/spack/spack/pull/49505>`_). The "
"``abstract`` key was added for abstract specs before the release of Spack "
"v1.0 (`#49756 <https://github.com/spack/spack/pull/49756>`_). The keys "
"``abstract_hash``, ``compiler_flags``, ``when``, and ``propagation`` were "
"added later for abstract specs, without a new version (`#52788 <https://"
"github.com/spack/spack/pull/52788>`_). The keys ``propagated_parameters`` "
"and ``propagated_abstract`` were added in the same way (`#52963 <https://"
"github.com/spack/spack/pull/52963>`_)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/specfile.rst:175
msgid "**Version 4** *(Spack v0.21)*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/specfile.rst:176
msgid ""
"Virtuals are recorded on the edges of the DAG (`#34821 <https://github.com/"
"spack/spack/pull/34821>`_). The dependency types of each entry move to "
"``parameters.deptypes``, next to the new ``parameters.virtuals``. The "
"``propagate`` key was added in Spack v0.23 for abstract specs, without a new "
"version (`#47351 <https://github.com/spack/spack/pull/47351>`_)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/specfile.rst:180
msgid "**Version 3** *(Spack v0.18)*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/specfile.rst:181
msgid ""
"The build hash and the full hash are removed (`#28504 <https://github.com/"
"spack/spack/pull/28504>`_). The structure is the same as in version 2, and "
"``hash`` becomes the DAG hash that includes build dependencies and the "
"package hash. In versions 1 and 2 the DAG hash includes only link and run "
"dependencies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/specfile.rst:185
msgid "**Version 2** *(Spack v0.17)*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/specfile.rst:186
msgid ""
"Installation prefixes move from ``spec.yaml`` to ``spec.json`` (`#22845 "
"<https://github.com/spack/spack/pull/22845>`_). The ``_meta.version`` key is "
"added, ``nodes`` becomes a list of dictionaries with a ``name`` key, "
"``dependencies`` becomes a list, and ``build_spec`` is added."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/specfile.rst:189
msgid "**Version 1** *(Spack v0.16 and earlier)*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/specfile.rst:190
msgid ""
"Spec files are YAML (``spec.yaml``), or JSON with the same structure. The "
"``spec`` key holds a list with one ``{<name>: <node>}`` entry for each node. "
"Dependencies are a dictionary keyed by name, with the hash of the dependency "
"and its ``type``. The hash of the dependency is stored under ``hash``, "
"``full_hash``, or ``build_hash``, depending on the version of Spack that "
"wrote the file."
msgstr ""
